# A global first bound inside a top-level if/try block is still a module
# binding; an inner function must mutate it, not shadow it. ouroboros's
# module-name pre-scan only saw direct top-level assigns.
#
# This file used to carry a second half doing the same through a top-level
# `for` body — at the v0.39.0 pin that is loop-local and errors on both sides
# (upstream triage: EigenScript#959), so it now lives as a must_reject case in
# test/run.sh, and this program is clean parity again.
if 1 == 1:
    counter is 0
define inc() as:
    counter is counter + 1
inc of null
inc of null
print of counter
